<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Tercan</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Tercan is a town in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/erzincan">Erzincan</a> province in eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/turkey">Turkey</a>, on the road between Erzincan and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/erzurum">Erzurum</a>. In the 12th century it belonged to the Saltukids of Erzurum, and its best-known monument is the tomb of Mama Hatun, a Saltukid ruler, built around 1200 within an unusual circular walled courtyard.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/tercan.jpg" alt="Tercan" width="320" height="212" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Dosseman · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Tercan_area_on_hill_2823.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
